  "id": "behavior-setting",
  "term": "behavior setting",
  "definition": "In ecological psychology, a behavior setting is the linked pattern between recurring, longer-term behavior and the material features of an environment. The term emphasizes that behavior and setting are understood together as a dynamic relationship rather than as separate factors.",
